{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"challenge_brief","title":"Challenge brief","description":"The challenge as Markdown: the task, the websites, the rules and limits, the run contract (environment, browsers and time limits), how answers are submitted and scored, and the answer schema. Ranking: eligible answers first, then quality, then LLM cost × run time. About 6k tokens.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"challenge":{"type":"string","description":"The challenge id; the platform's default when left out"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Challenge brief","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"list_runs","title":"List runs","description":"Your team's recent test runs and scored runs, newest first: id, kind, status, quality and eligibility, LLM cost, run time, start and the package (its SHA-256 and label). Use get_run for one run, diagnose_run for why it failed.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["all","test","scored"],"description":"Which runs (default all)"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":50,"description":"How many (default 15)"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"List runs","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"get_run","title":"Get a run","description":"One run in full: status, phase and failure, its place in the queue or the free models' warm-up while it waits, phase starts on the run's clock, the package, LLM calls by model with failures and queue waits, the score with points per field (test runs), the recordings, the answer it entered, and the run page URL (?t=mm:ss opens the replay there). About 1–2k tokens.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Get a run","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"diagnose_run","title":"Diagnose a run","description":"Why a run failed and what to do next, in one call: the failure class and whether a rerun as it is would help, the last 20 lines of stdout and stderr, the answer, model errors by status, stretches over 60 s with no input, no screen change and no model call, and browsers whose screen froze. About 2–3k tokens.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Diagnose a run","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"run_logs","title":"Query run logs","description":"A run's log lines, in time order, each with its time on the run's clock and its stream. Streams: stdout and stderr (your agent system), setup (the platform: install, the free models' warm-up), input (what the browsers received; run_inputs reads them better, so they're left out unless you ask). Narrow with from/to (e.g. from 02:10 to 02:40), grep, browser; tail for the last lines; page with after. About 30 tokens a line.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"from":{"type":"string","description":"The earliest time, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works."},"to":{"type":"string","description":"The latest time, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works."},"stream":{"type":"string","description":"Only these streams, comma-separated: stdout, stderr, setup, input; \"all\" is every one. Default: stdout, stderr and setup."},"grep":{"type":"string","description":"Only lines containing this text, case-insensitive; a|b matches either"},"browser":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":4,"description":"Only the platform's lines about this browser (its inputs, a browser it stopped)"},"tail":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"description":"Only the last n matching lines"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"description":"Lines per page (default 200)"},"after":{"type":"string","description":"Continue after a previous page: its `next` value"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Query run logs","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"run_llm_calls","title":"Model calls","description":"Every model call of a run, one line each: time on the run's clock, latency, queue wait (hosted models), model, status, tokens (cached), cost and id. The header has the time in calls, p50/p95 latency, the most calls at once, failures by status and the hosted models' queue waits. Filter by from/to, model and status (ok, error, all); page with after. About 35 tokens a call.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"from":{"type":"string","description":"The earliest start, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works."},"to":{"type":"string","description":"The latest start, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"Only models whose provider/model contains this, e.g. qwen"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["ok","error","all"],"description":"Which calls to list (default all)"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"description":"Calls per page (default 100)"},"after":{"type":"string","description":"Continue after a call id (c_123), e.g. the previous page's next"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Model calls","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"run_profile","title":"Where the time went","description":"Where a run's time went, bucket by bucket (30 s, 1 min or 5 min): per browser, its inputs and how long its screen was changing (– idle); model calls, seconds in calls and cost. Then the critical path: the longest stretches with nothing happening, the slowest calls, and when each browser went quiet. About 1.5–3k tokens.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"bucket":{"type":"string","enum":["30s","1m","5m"],"description":"Bucket size (default: by the run's length)"},"browser":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":4,"description":"Only this browser"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Where the time went","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"run_screenshot","title":"Browser screenshot at a time","description":"A browser's screen at a time in the run, cut from its recording, with the clicks just before it marked (red: the latest) and the log lines around it. browser \"all\" puts every browser in one 2×2 image; frames {from, to, every} makes a filmstrip of up to 9 frames in one image. While a run is still going there is no recording yet: it shows the latest live frame. About 1.5k tokens an image.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"at":{"type":"string","description":"When, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works. Not needed with frames."},"browser":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"Which browser, 1–4 (default 1), or \"all\" for every browser at once"},"frames":{"type":"object","description":"A filmstrip instead of one frame: {from, to, every}, times on the run's clock (every: e.g. 10s)","properties":{"from":{"type":"string"},"to":{"type":"string"},"every":{"type":"string"}}},"marks":{"type":"boolean","description":"Mark the clicks recorded just before (default true)"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Browser screenshot at a time","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"run_inputs","title":"Recorded browser inputs","description":"What the agent system did in the browsers, as the platform recorded it: clicks and taps with x,y on the 1280×800 display (Chrome's bar included), drags, scrolls and typing, each with its time on the run's clock, in time order. Typed text shows, with keys and tokens masked. Pair a time with run_screenshot to see the screen then.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"browser":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":4,"description":"Only this browser"},"from":{"type":"string","description":"The earliest time, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works."},"to":{"type":"string","description":"The latest time, on the run's clock, as the run page and run_logs show it: mm:ss or h:mm:ss (seconds may have a fraction), 3m20s, or seconds; a minus is before the start. An ISO 8601 time also works."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"description":"Inputs per page (default 200)"},"after":{"type":"string","description":"Continue after a previous page: its `next` value"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Recorded browser inputs","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"compare_runs","title":"Compare two runs","description":"Two runs side by side (A, then B, and how B differs): package, status, quality, time, cost, cost × time, calls and failures, phase times, calls and cost per model, the score's points per field that changed, and the answer's fields that changed. About 1–2k tokens.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"a":{"type":"string","description":"The first run (A). A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"b":{"type":"string","description":"The second run (B), e.g. after a change. A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"}},"required":["a","b"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Compare two runs","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"wait_for_run","title":"Wait for a run","description":"Wait until a run is running (its agent system has started) or done, then say how it stands; while it waits it sends progress. Gives up after timeout_s (default 50 s, at most 600: raise it if your client allows long tool calls) and says where the run is, so you can call it again.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"until":{"type":"string","enum":["running","done"],"description":"What to wait for (default done)"},"timeout_s":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":600,"description":"How long to wait at most (default 50)"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Wait for a run","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"list_submissions","title":"List submissions","description":"Your team's scored submissions, newest first: id, when, review status, any organizer note, status, quality and eligibility with cost and time, and the package. The reviewer's reasons stay with the organizers. get_submission shows one with its runs.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"challenge":{"type":"string","description":"The challenge id; the platform's default when left out"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":50,"description":"How many (default 10)"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"List submissions","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"get_submission","title":"Get a submission","description":"One scored submission: its review status and any organizer note (the reviewer's reasons stay with the organizers), its runs with their status, place in the queue and score, and the package. Takes a sub_ id.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"submission_id":{"type":"string","description":"A submission id (sub_...) from list_submissions"}},"required":["submission_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Get a submission","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"run_package","title":"Run package","description":"The package a test run, scored run or submission of your team used, exactly as uploaded: its SHA-256 and label, agent.json, and every file's path and size (never the contents). With out, it also saves the .tar.gz in that folder, checked against its SHA-256; unpack it with tar to read the files. About 15 tokens a file.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: the package it submitted, which its runs ran)"},"out":{"type":"string","description":"A folder to save the .tar.gz in: an absolute path, or relative to where this server runs (usually your project); made if missing"}},"required":["run_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Run package","readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"leaderboard","title":"Leaderboard","description":"The leaderboard (on the public dataset during the hackathon) with each entry's cost × time and the Pareto front, your team's rank and the gap to the next rank. compare_run: where one of your runs would rank if it were your team's entry. Ranking: eligible first, then quality, then LLM cost × run time.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"challenge":{"type":"string","description":"The challenge id; the platform's default when left out"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"description":"How many entries (default 10)"},"compare_run":{"type":"string","description":"One of your runs to place on the board. A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Leaderboard","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"models","title":"Free models","description":"The models the organizers host for free, whether each is up, and how to call them from your computer through `atira models proxy` (the variables to export). Calls from your computer are free, recorded and never ranked.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Free models","readOnlyHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"test_run","title":"Start a test run","description":"Pack a folder and start a test run: it runs once in the same sandbox as scored runs, on the public scenario, and never counts for the leaderboard. Returns the run id, its place in the queue, the package's SHA-256 and label (the git commit by default) and its page; then wait_for_run, run_logs and run_screenshot.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"dir":{"type":"string","description":"The package folder, with agent.json at its root: an absolute path, or relative to where this server runs (usually your project). .gitignore is respected."},"label":{"type":"string","description":"A short label for this package (at most 100 characters), shown with the run; the folder's git commit when left out (with -dirty for uncommitted changes)"},"challenge":{"type":"string","description":"The challenge id; the platform's default when left out"}},"required":["dir"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Start a test run","readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"cancel_run","title":"Cancel a run","description":"Cancel one of your team's test or scored runs that has not finished: its sandbox is removed and the run fails as cancelled; its logs stay. A cancelled scored run doesn't come back, so this needs confirm: true; ask the person first for a scored run.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"run_id":{"type":"string","description":"A run id (run_...) from list_runs, a test run id (reh_...), or a submission id (sub_...: its latest run)"},"confirm":{"type":"boolean","description":"Must be true: the person asked for this run to be cancelled"}},"required":["run_id","confirm"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Cancel a run","readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"submit","title":"Submit for a ranked run","description":"Pack a folder and submit it for a scored run. This is public and can't be undone: it is reviewed, run once on the public dataset and ranked on the public leaderboard under the team's name, and the latest submission that passes review goes into the final run on the private dataset. Before calling, tell the person exactly that and get an explicit yes for this package, then call with confirm: true. Use test_run to try a package.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"dir":{"type":"string","description":"The package folder, with agent.json at its root: an absolute path, or relative to where this server runs (usually your project). .gitignore is respected."},"confirm":{"type":"boolean","description":"Must be true, and only after the person explicitly agreed to this public scored submission, which can't be undone"},"label":{"type":"string","description":"A short label for this package (at most 100 characters), shown with the run; the folder's git commit when left out (with -dirty for uncommitted changes)"},"challenge":{"type":"string","description":"The challenge id; the platform's default when left out"}},"required":["dir","confirm"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"title":"Submit for a ranked run","readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}}]}}

